      "ts": 1790180100.178472,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "I checked the three round-3 findings against the current code in wt/T-1274. Only those three fixes were reviewed: the diff shown was truncated, so the rest of the 725 hidden lines, the tests and the acceptance list were not read, and I did not run the tests. (1) decision_log.recent in grouped mode now returns immediately for empty subjects. It keeps at most `limit` rows per subject and stops after GROUPED_SCAN_LIMIT lines read, whether or not applied rows were found. (2) daemon.py resets steering_refusal_reasons to None whenever the mode is not active, both in _steering_decisions and in steering_tick, so a later return to active notifies again. (3) safe_scope returns the scope entries unchanged when no worktree is known, with no cwd fallback. When a worktree is known, it still rejects absolute paths, '..' parts and symlink escapes. I found no problems in the trust boundaries or privileges in these hunks.",
        "verdict": "approve",
